# Frozen single-owner matrix admission review — 22 October 2026

**Decision: performance parity is not established; keep the draft stack held and unmerged.** Both required dense complete operations are slower than same-machine main and published 0.1.0 at pooled p50 and p95. Other required families contain gains, but those cannot offset a failed family. The latest instruction ends optimization only at verified parity or better across the fixed seven families, with no later boost waves. This review admits no further product wave or favorable rerun.

## Identity and measurement boundary

The frozen product commit is `dec7509b3a18b2d71e27de023419f45c32fb10e7`; its archive SHA-256 is `06fe22b7f05dceb27f59b2e82d33fab541c8cee04c37b1a1ccdf078f6ecdc9be`. The freeze records all 713 tracked Glyph files matching the pre-commit product snapshot, and the named Wasm executable matching shipping shaper SHA-256 `66e6c46357030d8457a8568af303d8552b16a68f0c3815877d01d634996bbffb`. Main is commit `4e25a96a57462fef5ad0d19065a822695b480f60`, archive `bbb3375c08fb3db8186ec10e4b766b7170632f7601eb1ec0e90be0197f22eb20`. Published 0.1.0 archive is `6e2bf7bdef50ec528a4e4799b8f067e81335388265fbb4950cbbcf08f840581b`.

One full 145-identity candidate capture used eight blocks and single-call sampling under Labs 0.9.0, harness digest `a89c95dd78c46dde9d10cd7698912ce7f4507b9bfd26c4d1fdfa8b4b5cb6ec1b`. Its raw `candidate.json` SHA-256 is `3f6e73670c82af0e78dcff1b6aebb90f73084a4e55717d45132b0da4298a5fb8` in the original capture **and both comparisons**. Only each control was newly timed. Main raw baseline SHA-256 is `804103028a3d039cdf9a1e00d9e8bf4260eb5d538176448ce3e2524919d2dda3`; published raw baseline SHA-256 is `95ff27780366f454fdf4faee4c32d249e94754512b228ad21163445ae87af13a`. All runs report Apple M4, arm64 Darwin, Node 24.18.0, the same suite, blocks and package digest. They were separate runs on the same machine, not interleaved paired callbacks.

Every latency below is an **absolute complete-operation** pooled normalized Labs yield sample in milliseconds: sort an arm's samples and take nearest-rank `sample[ceil(q*N)-1]` for p50/p95. These values differ from Labs' block-estimator p50 changes and its console p99 column. Setters and publication are included where the named operation calls them. The matrix is Node package timing, not GPU time, displayed frame pacing or a browser-render result.

## Fixed-family evidence

The table selects decisive or representative identities; the raw matrix retains every identity. Each cell is **p50 / p95 ms**, ordered main, published, frozen candidate.

| Fixed family / exact operation | Main | Published 0.1.0 | Candidate | Admission reading |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
| 1. Long edits/Unicode/shape/flow: long unsafe-boundary paragraph reflow | 0.423042 / 0.658167 | 0.542000 / 0.743500 | 0.983625 / 1.746708 | Slower against both; other long-edit rows also vary. |
| 2. Dense preparation/publication: rewrite 512 labels in one group | 7.602375 / 8.926250 | 8.143042 / 12.271250 | 10.295208 / 117.498792 | Included and slower against both. |
| 2. Dense preparation/publication: publish 1,024 retained Text instances | 16.547042 / 18.207875 | 16.685583 / 18.421541 | 19.547625 / 22.203416 | Included and slower against both. |
| 3. Width/cold/inspection: mount and publish a 22k-glyph paragraph | 18.208916 / 19.312959 | 19.349084 / 20.380625 | 21.120708 / 23.615708 | Cold complete operation slower against both. |
| 3. Width/cold/inspection: measurement after width change | 0.917667 / 1.200542 | 0.988000 / 1.259208 | 1.359166 / 4.992542 | Slower; per-glyph inspection after width change improved (below). |
