Other preserved complete-operation gains include 1,000 labels with 100 immediate edits, measurements and publication (main `100.175834 / 159.389625`, published `163.723333 / 178.807292`, candidate `19.859459 / 52.354542` ms); interleaved edit-read publication (main `135.268958 / 180.572500`, published `193.260042 / 205.930083`, candidate `49.777333 / 78.359875`); and scattered 8,192-paint-span setter plus publication (main `21.201292 / 22.535416`, published `43.506000 / 46.799792`, candidate `15.734666 / 18.137333`). Per-glyph inspection after width change is also faster (`7.429167 / 10.431250` main, `9.545000 / 11.243334` published, `4.864209 / 8.399000` candidate). These gains are retained evidence, not a substitute for the adverse rows.

## Exclusions, calibration and inference

Main matches all 145 candidate identities; Labs compares 140: 57 faster, 39 slower, 44 neutral, **five clock-confounded skips**. Those skips are 100-label first color-only scene publication; 100-label first color-only engine publication; 100-label separated balanced grow-shrink-space scene publication; one-label first set+measure; and 100-label first set+measure+scene-publication. Published 0.1.0 documents **two unavailable outline identities**: copy per-glyph metrics with outlines after text change, and read every outline from an unchanged copy. Of the remaining 143 matched identities, Labs compares 134: 78 faster, 29 slower, 27 neutral, **nine clock-confounded skips**. They are trailing-span mutation across 1,000 formatted labels; 10-label first color-only scene publication; 100-label first length-changing scene publication; 1,000-label no-op scene traversal; relayout after font-size change; measurement of 100 unchanged labels; sparse borrow of one among 1,000 labels; common-safe word-wrap reflow; and issue-216 reporter workaround. Both manifests show zero baseline-check failures and zero timing-mode mismatches. Neither aggregate wins nor neutral labels prove fixed-family parity; skipped required rows cannot be counted as passing.

Labs flagged 90 candidate identities as noisy and reported **67.6% candidate software-calibration drift**. This calibration is not a hardware clock measurement. An unrelated Vite process was present in the pre-run load snapshot; neither that snapshot nor the matrix proves contention during a particular sample. Candidate dense512 has 128 samples, main 200, published 128. Its first block median is 113.293458 ms, while its other seven medians run 9.190500–12.660042 ms. The published and main control tails are lower, but Labs stores globally sorted samples: the raw receipt does not assign each tail sample to that block. The large p95 is an observed admission failure, not proof that the patch caused a 117 ms intrinsic tail or that machine load caused it. The maintained 512 and 1,024 fixtures also differ beyond count, so their p95 inversion is not a controlled count-scaling result.

Shipping shaper is 1,610,555 raw / 599,761 Node-gzip bytes, +148,550 / +58,398 versus main. Candidate JavaScript totals 876,353 raw and 299,207 bytes summed across individually gzipped members, versus main 864,307 / 295,869. These size observations do not rescue latency parity. Exact candidate-owned Rust allocator accounting exists for named operations, but is not yet a paired main/published allocation comparison; exact Glyph-owned JavaScript and GPU buffer accounting is absent. Whole-process memory receipts are excluded by the current policy. The matched actual-browser 512/1,024 diagnostic is a separate pending phase/count investigation and cannot replace the fixed seven-family matrix. Existing profiles are load-confounded and cannot causally assign the current matrix's dense deficit. No new product change, control timing, browser execution or memory gate was performed for this review.

Evidence: `matrix-candidate/{manifest.json,candidate.json,absolute-results.json}`; `matrix-main-final/{manifest.json,baseline.json,candidate.json,summary.md,comparison.txt}`; `matrix-published-final/{manifest.json,baseline.json,candidate.json,summary.md,comparison.txt}`; `dense-tail-analysis.json`; `freeze.json`; the current held-single-owner report and predeclared seven-family reconciliation. Published runner receipt `../boundary-20261022-matrix-published-final/result.json` exited 0 at 2026-10-22T16:49:15Z.
